WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.327 --> 00:00:14.289
The ghost spoke again, and his voice was quiet and low.

2
00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:17.931
"Have you ever read the old prophecy on the library window?"

3
00:00:18.331 --> 00:00:18.791
he asked.

4
00:00:19.412 --> 00:00:23.794
"Oh, often," said Virginia, turning from the tapestries on the walls to look at him.

5
00:00:24.595 --> 00:00:29.610
And she recited the verse from heart: When a golden girl can win Prayer from out the lips

6
00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:36.595
of sin, When the barren almond bears, And a little child gives away its tears, Then shall all

7
00:00:36.635 --> 00:00:39.697
the house be still And peace come to Canterville.

8
00:00:39.717 --> 00:00:42.819
"But I don't know what it means," she added.

9
00:00:42.839 --> 00:00:49.264
"It means," he said sadly, "that you must weep with me for my sins and pray with me

10
00:00:49.324 --> 00:00:54.367
for my soul, and if you have always been sweet and gentle and good, the Angel of Death

11
00:00:54.407 --> 00:00:55.428
will have mercy on me."

12
00:00:56.496 --> 00:00:59.958
A cold shudder ran through her, and she thought gravely for a moment.

13
00:01:00.558 --> 00:01:01.638
At last she stood up.

14
00:01:02.238 --> 00:01:06.660
"I am not afraid," she said firmly, "and I will ask the angel to have mercy on you."

15
00:01:07.761 --> 00:01:12.863
The ghost rose from his seat, and taking her hand, he bent over it with old-fashioned grace and

16
00:01:12.923 --> 00:01:13.323
kissed it.

17
00:01:14.303 --> 00:01:19.746
His fingers were as cold as ice, and his lips burned like fire, but Virginia did not tremble.

18
00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:25.128
Then, clutching her hand more tightly, Sir Simon of Canterville muttered an incantation.

19
00:01:25.948 --> 00:01:30.010
A cold, dark passage opened in the wall, and he pulled her quickly into it.

20
00:01:30.871 --> 00:01:36.314
As they passed out of the tapestry chamber, Virginia looked desperately over her shoulder and saw the figures

21
00:01:36.374 --> 00:01:37.695
in the tapestries behind her.

22
00:01:38.975 --> 00:01:42.177
The animals and huntsmen called out, "Beware, Virginia!

23
00:01:42.437 --> 00:01:44.178
Your family may never find you again."

24
00:01:45.179 --> 00:01:48.020
At dinnertime, Virginia's chair at the dining table stood empty.

25
00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.781
"Where is your sister?"

26
00:01:50.121 --> 00:01:51.602
Mr. Otis asked Washington.

27
00:01:51.622 --> 00:01:56.256
"She's probably in the garden getting flowers for the table," Washington answered.

28
00:01:56.276 --> 00:01:57.437
"I'll go get her."

29
00:01:58.217 --> 00:01:59.257
But he couldn't find her.

30
00:01:59.997 --> 00:02:03.118
When he came back, the family decided to look through the castle.

31
00:02:03.638 --> 00:02:06.599
Everyone spread out, calling Virginia's name in all the rooms.

32
00:02:07.259 --> 00:02:11.761
When the castle was thoroughly searched and there was no trace of her anywhere, they met in the

33
00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:14.101
library. They were all a little worried.

34
00:02:14.802 --> 00:02:18.083
It was now evening, and the light outside the tall windows was fading.

35
00:02:19.003 --> 00:02:22.604
"Perhaps she didn't come home after her ride with the duke," suggested Mr.

36
00:02:22.704 --> 00:02:25.745
Otis. "Maybe the Gypsies have taken her!"

37
00:02:26.365 --> 00:02:26.905
cried Mrs.

38
00:02:27.025 --> 00:02:27.865
Otis anxiously.

39
00:02:27.885 --> 00:02:30.647
"Let's not get frantic," Mr.

40
00:02:30.727 --> 00:02:31.527
Otis said calmly.

41
00:02:31.547 --> 00:02:34.148
"I'll ride over to the Cheshire estate right now.

42
00:02:34.468 --> 00:02:35.308
I'm sure she's there."

43
00:02:36.169 --> 00:02:40.731
While he was gone, Washington took a lamp outside and searched the castle grounds.

44
00:02:41.331 --> 00:02:45.072
His mother and the twins searched inside again, opening every closet and cupboard.

45
00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:47.253
A short while later, Mr.

46
00:02:47.353 --> 00:02:51.455
Otis returned with the Duke of Cheshire, and both their faces were creased with worry.

47
00:02:52.095 --> 00:02:56.545
When he had heard that Virginia was missing, the young duke had insisted on riding back to help

48
00:02:56.585 --> 00:02:57.145
with the search.

49
00:02:58.086 --> 00:03:02.588
On the way, they had stopped by the Gypsy camp, only to discover that the Gypsies had gone.

50
00:03:03.168 --> 00:03:07.690
It was evident that the Gypsies had left in a hurry, as their fire was still smoking and

51
00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:09.410
some plates had been left on the grass.

52
00:03:10.871 --> 00:03:11.711
Straight away, Mr.

53
00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:17.694
Otis sent Washington off to the train station to inquire if anyone fitting Virginia's description had been seen

54
00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:22.376
on the platform and to dispatch telegrams to the police in all the surrounding districts.

55
00:03:23.456 --> 00:03:27.838
Then he and the duke headed out into the night again to ride for Bexley, a village about

56
00:03:27.918 --> 00:03:31.059
four miles away that was known as a gathering place for Gypsies.

57
00:03:31.579 --> 00:03:34.581
They found not the slightest hint or sign of the missing girl.

58
00:03:35.541 --> 00:03:40.683
The Gypsies, too, were distressed to hear of Virginia's disappearance, as she had always said hello when she

59
00:03:40.723 --> 00:03:43.544
passed their camp, and they remembered her smiling face.

60
00:03:44.665 --> 00:03:46.425
Tired and dejected, Mr.

61
00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:50.087
Otis and the duke returned home to find the rest of the family, including Mrs.

62
00:03:50.207 --> 00:03:52.468
Umney, waiting at the castle gate with lanterns.

63
00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:54.781
There was nothing more that could be done.

64
00:03:55.661 --> 00:04:00.464
So everyone went inside to eat a sad and quiet meal, hoping that they would hear something from

65
00:04:00.504 --> 00:04:01.004
the police.

66
00:04:02.225 --> 00:04:06.007
Just as they were passing out of the dining room, the tall clock in the hall began to

67
00:04:06.047 --> 00:04:11.310
strike midnight, and when the last stroke sounded, they heard a crash and a sudden shrill cry.

68
00:04:11.971 --> 00:04:16.633
Dreadful thunder shook the castle, a piece of wooden paneling flew off the wall at the top of

69
00:04:16.673 --> 00:04:21.456
the staircase, and out onto the landing stepped Virginia, looking very pale and white.

70
00:04:22.556 --> 00:04:25.597
In her hands was a small jewelry box of tarnished silver.

71
00:04:26.518 --> 00:04:28.198
In a moment, they had all rushed up to her.

72
00:04:28.719 --> 00:04:32.820
Everyone hugged her, even the twins, and the young duke kissed her several times on the cheek.

73
00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:35.902
"Thank God you are safe," murmured Mrs.

74
00:04:36.002 --> 00:04:38.483
Otis as she put her arm around the trembling girl.

75
00:04:39.303 --> 00:04:40.063
"Where have you been?"

76
00:04:40.724 --> 00:04:41.164
said Mr.

77
00:04:41.244 --> 00:04:42.204
Otis rather angrily.

78
00:04:42.224 --> 00:04:45.045
"We've been riding all over the country looking for you!"

79
00:04:46.066 --> 00:04:49.307
"Father," said Virginia quietly, "I have been with the ghost.

80
00:04:50.227 --> 00:04:52.733
He is finally at peace, and you must come see him.

81
00:04:53.373 --> 00:04:57.355
He was really sorry for all that he had done, and he gave me this box of beautiful

82
00:04:57.415 --> 00:04:58.575
jewels before he left."

83
00:04:59.315 --> 00:05:01.276
The whole family gazed at her in amazement.

84
00:05:01.696 --> 00:05:06.138
With a serious look, she turned around and led them through the opening in the wall, and down

85
00:05:06.198 --> 00:05:07.499
a narrow secret corridor.

86
00:05:08.419 --> 00:05:13.662
Washington followed with a lighted candle, and when they came to the end, the flickering light showed a

87
00:05:13.722 --> 00:05:15.743
low room with one tiny barred window.

88
00:05:16.583 --> 00:05:18.704
Stretched out on the floor was a gaunt skeleton.

89
00:05:19.388 --> 00:05:24.490
Its ankle was chained to the stone wall, and its long, fleshless fingers seemed to grasp at a

90
00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:27.712
dusty, mold-filled jug placed just out of its reach.

91
00:05:28.352 --> 00:05:30.793
Virginia knelt down and touched the skeleton tenderly.

92
00:05:30.813 --> 00:05:35.275
"This is where Sir Simon died a horrible death by starvation," she explained.

93
00:05:36.175 --> 00:05:39.977
One of the twins went to the small window to look outside and figure out which wing of

94
00:05:40.017 --> 00:05:41.017
the castle they were in.

95
00:05:41.037 --> 00:05:43.698
"Look at that," he called.

96
00:05:43.718 --> 00:05:45.659
"The old almond tree has blossomed.

97
00:05:46.199 --> 00:05:47.740
I can see the flowers in the moonlight."

98
00:05:48.628 --> 00:05:53.529
"The angel has forgiven him," said Virginia, and as she slowly rose to her feet, the rest of

99
00:05:53.569 --> 00:05:54.910
her family looked at her in wonder.

100
00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:59.991
Four days after these curious incidents, there was a funeral at Canterville Castle.

101
00:06:00.632 --> 00:06:04.933
Eight black horses pulled an old-fashioned carriage that carried an ornately carved coffin.

102
00:06:06.133 --> 00:06:10.674
Draped over the coffin was a rich purple cloth embroidered with the Canterville coat of arms.

103
00:06:11.475 --> 00:06:16.716
Lord and Lady Canterville came up to the castle to lead the procession for their ancient ancestor, and

104
00:06:16.756 --> 00:06:18.437
Virginia rode with them in their carriage.

105
00:06:19.017 --> 00:06:23.418
The coffin was lowered into a deep grave under the spreading branches of the almond tree in a

106
00:06:23.478 --> 00:06:25.719
quiet corner of the graveyard behind the castle.

107
00:06:26.559 --> 00:06:32.841
Years later the Duke of Cheshire and his beautiful duchess were visiting Canterville Castle to see Virginia's parents.

108
00:06:34.341 --> 00:06:39.543
The young couple had been married the year after Sir Simon's funeral, and at the ceremony everyone had

109
00:06:39.603 --> 00:06:41.563
admired the rare jewels she wore.

110
00:06:42.364 --> 00:06:48.138
Whenever she visited the castle, Virginia walked the quiet path to the almond tree to lay a flower

111
00:06:48.238 --> 00:06:49.579
on Sir Simon's gravestone.

112
00:06:50.319 --> 00:06:55.182
That evening, as she and her husband sat together in the moonlight, a nightingale began to sing in

113
00:06:55.222 --> 00:06:56.143
the branches above.

114
00:06:56.963 --> 00:07:02.106
Virginia quietly remembered the ghost's description of the Garden of Death, when her husband took hold of her

115
00:07:02.146 --> 00:07:07.589
hand. "Virginia," he said, "you never told me what happened when you were locked up with the ghost."

116
00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:09.970
"Please don't ask me, dear.

117
00:07:10.491 --> 00:07:12.712
It is something I cannot tell," she said.

118
00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:14.461
She looked at him and paused.

119
00:07:14.481 --> 00:07:20.864
"Except to say, he made me see what life is, and what death means, and why love is

120
00:07:20.924 --> 00:07:21.885
stronger than both."
